</form><html xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:math="java.lang.Math" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xs="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:fo="http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Format" xmlns:fn="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-functions" xmlns:xdt="http://www.w3.org/2005/02/xpath-datatypes" xmlns:caml="http://lc.ca.gov/legalservices/schemas/caml.1#" xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><title>SR131:v99#DOCUMENT</title><meta name="dc:identifier" content="SR131"/><meta name="dc:title" content="SR &#xA;              131-&#xA;                INTRODUCED&#xA;              "/><meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html;charset=utf-8"/></head><body><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Start</h2></span><div id="bill_all" align="justify"><div id="about"><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td align="center"/></tr></tbody></table></div><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><font size="3" style="FONT-FAMILY: MinionPC, Arial Unicode MS">
                    CALIFORNIA LEGISLATURE—
                    2025–2026 REGULAR SESSION</font></div><br clear="all"/><span id="bill_house_num"><div style="float: left; width:50%; font-weight: bold; "><span style="text-transform: uppercase; text-align:left;width:50%;"><b>
                Senate Resolution
              </b></span></div><div style="float:right; width:50%; text-align:right;"><span style="text-transform: uppercase;"><b>No. 131</b></span></div></span><hr/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><table style="border-collapse: collapse" cellSpacing="0" align="center" role="presentation"><tbody><tr><td id="bill_authors" align="center"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Introduced by Senator Durazo<br/>(Coauthor: Senator Richardson)<br/></span></td></tr><tr><td id="bill_intro_date" align="center" class="textcenter"><br/>August 03, 2026</td></tr></tbody></table></div><hr/><br clear="all"/><div id="title"><span style="font-weight:normal;font-size:0.9em;"> Relative to Suicide Prevention Awareness Month. </span></div><br clear="all"/><br clear="all"/><div align="center"><h2>LEGISLATIVE COUNSEL'S DIGEST</h2></div><br/><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0"><span id="subject">SR 131, as introduced, Durazo.
                          </span></div><div><span id="digesttext"/></div><span class="hidden"><h2>Digest Key</h2></span></div><hr/><span class="hidden"><h2>Bill Text</h2></span><span class="Resolution" title="source: /caml:MeasureDoc/caml:Resolution&#xA;    "><span class="Whereas" id="id_12DD6BFB-76E1-46E5-BF33-E152A3A1E172"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, September is recognized nationally as Suicide Prevention Awareness Month, a time to advance public understanding of suicide prevention, to reduce the stigma that prevents people from seeking help, and to affirm that support is available to anyone in crisis; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_D4120132-8880-4093-9DEE-83A21E04EB49"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Suicide is a serious public health concern that affects individuals, families, and communities across California, and timely access to compassionate mental health and crisis care saves lives; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_8DEF6BDB-C465-4235-A7AA-268281083D91"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Mental health, substance use, and suicidal crises are deeply connected, and a whole-person approach that addresses these needs together strengthens prevention and supports lasting recovery and well-being; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_14908189-6B3B-40D2-8985-359E282CD43D"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Community-based providers are essential partners to the state in delivering accessible mental health and crisis services, in reaching underserved communities, and in advancing the goals of California’s behavioral health system; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_0F5D950A-803D-4F95-A1A6-FF84463E2AB3"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, The California Association of Alcohol and Drug Program Executives represents more than 400 community-based substance use disorder treatment providers across California’s 58 counties, including Didi Hirsch Mental Health Services, and works to advance accessible behavioral health care for all Californians; and</div></span><span class="Whereas" id="id_0FAC562A-3AF8-4AAE-8F87-74EC080DC4B1"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">WHEREAS, Didi Hirsch Mental Health Services established the first 24-hour suicide prevention crisis line in the United States, and its Suicide Prevention Center continues to provide multilingual crisis call, chat, and text services via the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline, counseling for survivors of suicide attempts, and support for those who have lost loved ones to suicide; and</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_38E5B0CF-8007-48DF-BDFC-225A0563F712"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved by the Senate of the State of California, That the Legislature proclaims the month of September 2026 as Suicide Prevention Awareness Month in the State of California, recognizes the importance of suicide prevention and of access to mental health and crisis care, and affirms that support is available to all Californians, including through the 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline; and be it further</div></span><span class="Resolved" id="id_00DD2CF1-A714-402B-8B0B-77947AFCDACE"><div style="margin:0 0 1em 0;">Resolved, That the Secretary of the Senate transmit copies of this resolution to the author for appropriate distribution.</div></span></span></div></body></html>
